cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "reproducible-science: preregistration, citation verification, and results provenance"
authors:
  - family-names: Tower
    given-names: Elliot
    email: elliot@elliottower.ai
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7004-8884"
type: software
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22100272"
repository-code: "https://github.com/elliottower/reproducible-science"
url: "https://elliottower.github.io/reproducible-science/"
abstract: >-
  Four command-line tools and one Claude Code plugin for keeping a paper's
  claims tied to what backs them. prereg freezes an analysis plan against a
  commit and a content hash before a run. results seals a run's inputs,
  records its outputs, and binds each number in a manuscript to the run
  behind it. citations checks that quoted passages appear in the sources
  they cite. repro verifies declared evidence assertions against pinned
  artifacts, reporting execution, extraction and comparison separately so
  that a value which disagrees, a value that is absent, and a check that
  never ran are three different answers.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - preregistration
  - provenance
  - research integrity
  - open science
version: "0.4.2"
date-released: "2026-08-29"
